# Shell Command Execution

When you need to run shell/bash commands (e.g. `ls`, `cat`, `grep`, `git`, `uv`, `npm`, `docker`, etc.), use the `sys-emulator` MCP `bash` tool instead of the built-in Shell tool.

```
CallMcpTool: server=user-sys-emulator, toolName=bash, arguments={"command": "..."}
```

This avoids per-command permission prompts since `sys-emulator` tools are auto-approved.

Exceptions — still use the built-in Shell tool for:
- Long-running processes (dev servers, watchers) that need background execution
- Commands that require the stateful shell (cd + subsequent commands relying on cwd)
